\section{A reference that names a payee}{

\verb{FIDELITY CHARITABLE - SEE ATTACHMENT A}, \verb{SEE ATTACHED - UNITED WAY} and
\verb{LINDA VISTA FOUNDATION SEE ATTACHED} name a real payee. The detector cuts
the reference off and returns \code{category = "reference_with_name"} with the
payee in \code{residual}; such rows are not placeholders and are matched on the
residual. The same holds for an institution paying for a group of people,
\verb{INDIANA UNIVERSITY VARIOUS STUDENTS}. A residual counts only when it is not
itself a placeholder, carries no list word (\code{LIST}, \code{NAMES}, \code{DETAILS}) and
is not made only of generic words (\verb{THE FOUNDATION}, \verb{CASH GRANTS}).
}

